1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,687
"Just add PayNow."

2
00:00:01,687 --> 00:00:05,930
That was a real hawker-stall
requirements brief.

3
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:07,704
A coding agent will build it

4
00:00:07,704 --> 00:00:10,453
and guess what happens
when payment fails.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,660
SpecBuddy is the quality gate
before your coding agent.

6
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,733
It scores.

7
00:00:17,733 --> 00:00:19,626
It refuses ambiguity.

8
00:00:19,626 --> 00:00:21,706
Only the deterministic linter

9
00:00:21,706 --> 00:00:24,672
decides when a spec is ready.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,110
Four layers, one invariant.

11
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:31,111
A React frontend for review
and clarification.

12
00:00:31,111 --> 00:00:35,585
A FastAPI and SQLite backend
for transactional rewrites.

13
00:00:35,585 --> 00:00:39,962
A deterministic Python linter
enforces EARS and scores.

14
00:00:39,962 --> 00:00:42,110
Only the linter can certify.

15
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:44,443
The AI layer only proposes:

16
00:00:44,443 --> 00:00:48,333
exactly two mutually exclusive
rewrites, never a verdict.

17
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:52,355
That separation is
the core architecture.

18
00:00:52,355 --> 00:00:56,485
People review tradeoffs;
AI drafts bounded options.

19
00:00:56,485 --> 00:00:58,363
SpecBuddy gives
the final yes or no.

20
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,077
SpecBuddy catches weak requirements
before a coding agent starts building.

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,293
Here is a real heartland brief,
written like clients really write.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,277
SpecBuddy refuses it immediately:
score zero, twenty-two findings.

23
00:01:23,277 --> 00:01:27,024
It flags PayNow retry gaps
and missing PDPA consent.

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,885
The Mission Board turns issues
into a visible checklist.

25
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,461
Each finding has an exact line,
plus a fix or question.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,949
Apply one fix and one answer;
the findings count drops.

27
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,163
Accepted rewrites stay visible
and reversible.

28
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,267
Resolve the rest, and the spec
reaches CERTIFIED state.

29
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,949
One hundred out of one hundred:
CERTIFIED for agent handoff.

30
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,398
This is not marketing.
It is measured.

31
00:02:42,398 --> 00:02:45,425
Twenty-one adversarial
benchmark cases.

32
00:02:45,425 --> 00:02:48,240
Ten hostile briefs tested.
Zero crashes.

33
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:51,373
False positives dropped
from sixteen down to one.

34
00:02:51,373 --> 00:02:52,587
Zero regressions.

35
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,060
We built SpecBuddy using
a spec-driven workflow.

36
00:02:57,060 --> 00:03:02,340
Every new feature started
as a requirements document.

37
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:05,108
We ran each one through
SpecBuddy until it certified.

38
00:03:05,108 --> 00:03:09,927
The Clarify interaction
came from a certified spec.

39
00:03:09,927 --> 00:03:13,934
Tencent CodeBuddy implemented
the reserved frontend slice.

40
00:03:13,934 --> 00:03:17,109
The rule was explicit:
AI proposes.

41
00:03:17,109 --> 00:03:22,817
Only the deterministic linter
certifies.

42
00:03:22,817 --> 00:03:27,123
The practical lesson:
make the handoff measurable.

43
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:31,549
Review means changed files,
tests, and the gate.

44
00:03:31,549 --> 00:03:35,728
Accepted rewrites stay visible
for human review.

45
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,299
Built for Singapore agencies

46
00:03:39,299 --> 00:03:42,412
and SMEs commissioning
agent-built software.

47
00:03:42,412 --> 00:03:45,886
Also for BAs and PMs
writing their briefs.

48
00:03:45,886 --> 00:03:48,598
As a per-seat gate
with CI integration,

49
00:03:48,598 --> 00:03:53,123
deterministic verdicts are
what a CI pipeline can trust.

50
00:03:53,123 --> 00:03:55,448
The buyer does not need
another chatbot.

51
00:03:55,448 --> 00:03:57,907
They need an auditable
checkpoint before build.

52
00:03:59,000 --> 00:03:59,904
Next:

53
00:03:59,904 --> 00:04:02,761
specs directly from docs
and meeting notes,

54
00:04:02,761 --> 00:04:04,433
a CI gate mode,

55
00:04:04,433 --> 00:04:08,350
expanded rule packs for
PDPA and payments.

56
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:11,928
SpecBuddy moves into
daily delivery.

57
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,523
Same coding agent.

58
00:04:14,523 --> 00:04:15,631
Clearer specs in.

59
00:04:15,631 --> 00:04:16,951
Better software out.

60
00:04:16,951 --> 00:04:17,779
SpecBuddy.
